==========================================================================
 LAS parameter set: n=8 ell=7 kappa=60 gamma=230400  (N=256, Q=8380417)
==========================================================================
 10 runs x 1000 iters/op; mean +/- sample SD; single thread, -O3.

--- WHAT IS COMPARED (separate modules, matched parameters, shared primitives) ---
 BASE  (simplified Dilithium-style signature; NO adaptor statement):
   Sign     c = H(pk, w,   M)        Verify    c == H(pk, w',  M)
 LAS ADAPTOR (same scheme; statement/lock Y folded into the hash):
   PreSign  c = H(pk, w+Y, M)        PreVerify c == H(pk, w'+Y, M)
   Adapt    z = z_hat + y_witness    Ext       y_witness = z - z_hat
   Adapted sig clears ordinary Verify without an explicit +Y because
     A(z_hat+y) - c*t = (A*z_hat - c*t) + A*y = w' + Y    (Y = A*y).

--- COMPUTATION (microseconds, mean +/- sample SD) ---

 Base path (simplified Dilithium-style, c = H(pk, w, M); no Y):
   KeyGen       152.69 +/-   3.57
   Sign        1512.32 +/-  58.02
   Verify       375.23 +/-   8.73

 LAS adaptor path (Y folded into the hash, c = H(pk, w+Y, M)):
   PreSign     1449.94 +/-  30.35
   PreVerify    371.54 +/-   8.79
   Adapt        393.29 +/-   4.51
   Ext          138.74 +/-   0.62

 Adaptor overhead (adaptor op vs the base op it mirrors):
   PreSign   vs Sign      1449.94 vs  1512.32   (-4.1%)
   PreVerify vs Verify     371.54 vs   375.23   (-1.0%)
   Adapt     vs Verify     393.29 vs   375.23   (+4.8%)
   Ext       (separate)    138.74            (no base analogue)

--- COMMUNICATION (packed bytes) ---
   public key  pk          5888
   secret key  sk           960
   challenge   c             64
   response    z           9120   (99.3% of the signature)
   signature   (c,z)       9184
   statement   Y           5888
   pre-signature           9184
